sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as Thread
    participant Reg as Registers
    participant SMEM as Shared memory
    participant L2 as L2
    participant HBM as HBM
    participant NV as NVLink peer
    participant Host as Host RAM
    T->>Reg: ~1 cycle
    T->>SMEM: ~20 cycles
    T->>L2: ~200 cycles
    T->>HBM: ~400 cycles, but enormous bandwidth
    T->>NV: another GPU's memory, hundreds of GB/s
    T->>Host: over PCIe — an order of magnitude slower again
    Note over T,Host: every level down is ~10x. Arithmetic is cheap, moving bytes is not
    Note over NV,Host: NUMA matters — a GPU reading the wrong socket's RAM pays twice
